
========================================================================
P1  Even skew rank is not by itself the odd-support theorem
========================================================================
even support size 2: tournament payoff block mod 2 has full rank 2
even support size 4: tournament payoff block mod 2 has full rank 4
even support size 6: tournament payoff block mod 2 has full rank 6
An optimal support block must be singular; the mod-2 tournament form excludes even size.
n=3: all 8 tournaments; unique-support sizes=[1, 3]
n=4: all 64 tournaments; unique-support sizes=[1, 3]
n=5: all 1024 tournaments; unique-support sizes=[1, 3, 5]

========================================================================
P2  Pure optimum means Condorcet winner, not transitivity
========================================================================
4-vertex witness: 0 is Condorcet winner; 1->2->3->1 is a directed cycle.
The tournament is intransitive but its unique optimal support is {0}.
For interior replicator states, x_0' = x_0(1-x_0), so x_0 tends to 1.

========================================================================
P3  The correct dynamical hinge is a positive kernel vector
========================================================================
RPS has p=(1/3,1/3,1/3) in ker(M).
Hence d/dt sum_i p_i log(x_i)=p^T Mx=0; equivalently x0*x1*x2 is conserved.
Positive regular levels inside Delta^2 are periodic circles S^1, not a surface T^2.
hostile skew control column sums=[-2, 0, 2]; antisymmetry alone does not conserve the product.

========================================================================
P4  Closed torus, solid torus, and cutting sequence are different objects
========================================================================
T^1: Betti=[1, 1], chi=0
T^2: Betti=[1, 2, 1], chi=0
T^3: Betti=[1, 3, 3, 1], chi=0
T^4: Betti=[1, 4, 6, 4, 1], chi=0
T^5: Betti=[1, 5, 10, 10, 5, 1], chi=0
solid torus D^2 x S^1: Betti=[1,1], chi=0
boundary T^2: Betti=[1,2,1], chi=0; a perfect Morse function has counts 1,2,1
No computation here identifies bagel(n)-cake(n)=T_n-1 with either Euler characteristic.

========================================================================
P5  Three different sign actions
========================================================================
torus inversion on T^1: 2 fixed 2-torsion points
torus inversion on T^2: 4 fixed 2-torsion points
torus inversion on T^3: 8 fixed 2-torsion points
LRC far-set Fourier weights are even, not odd.
Vandermonde changes sign under a coordinate transposition.
Matrix complement M->-M, torus inversion, and permutation parity are distinct Z/2 actions.

========================================================================
SUMMARY
========================================================================
Exact survivors: skew rank parity; tournament-specific odd optimal support; torus Betti data;
the RPS positive-kernel invariant; torus-inversion fixed points; even LRC weights; and
alternating Vandermonde.  The one-hinge synthesis, pure<=>transitive claim, bagel Euler
bridge, and intransitivity=>toroidal recurrence claim are refuted.
